      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1907-08-31_WidnesExaminer_art0001" n="art0001">
        <head>ACCOMPANYING PROCESSEti CONSULT</head>
        <p>ACCOMPANYING PROCESSEti CONSULT</p>
        <p>W. J. BARNES,</p>
        <p>54, LEGH STREET, WARRINGTON.</p>
        <p>LARGE POSTERS JOHN WALKER &amp; CO., BEWSEY STREET, WARRINGTON.</p>
        <p>Mit</p>
        <p>No 1590</p>
        <p>WARRINGTON UNION.-TENDERS- PBRSONS WILLING to Contract for the supply of any of the undermentioued articles from Michaelmas to Lady Day next, to be delis erel free of expense at the Workhouse or Cottage Homes situateil at Padgate at such times and in such quantities as the Guardians or their officers may require are request.d to send in tenders to me on or before Tuesday, September 17th, 1907. Tenders are required for *— Milk for Workhouse (12 months) For 6 months : Coal And Slack Milk for Schools Clogs Fish and Ice Shoes and Slippers Groceries and Necessaries</p>
        <p>Coffins _ _ Batcher's Meat, &amp; Officer's Joints Brooms and Brushes Flour and Oatmeal Leather and Shoemakers' Bread for Cottage Homes</p>
        <p>2tirecessaries Tailors Goods</p>
        <p>Drspery Wines and Spirits</p>
        <p>Separate Tenders must be sent for the Workhouse and Cottage Homes, and samples of the article s required can be seen at either institution. The fuel to t4e suppllesi must be according to the specifica- tion as set forth on the tender form and quotations must be made fs,r delivery either to the new siding adjoining the Workhouse or by cart. Forms of tender, and instructions to persons tendering, which must be strictly complied wit b,or any other information may be obtained from the Master of the Workhouse, and the Superintendent of the Cottage Homes respectively, between the hours of 10 a.m. and 4 p.m. The Guardians do not necessarily bind themselves to accept the lowest or any tender, By order, JAMBS C. SUTTON, Clerk to the Guardians. Bewley Chamber!, August, 1907.</p>
        <p>COUNTY OF OHIMBR.</p>
        <p>KNUTSFORD PARLTAMETARY DIVISION.</p>
        <p>REGISTRATION OF PARLIAMENTARY ELECTOR 4, COUNTY ELECTORS AND PAROCHIAL ELECT° R 5,1907. N OTICE I LINEKBY GIVEN, that CLEMEN I J... 1 IMPHINSTONE LLOYD, ESQHIRE, having been appointed one of the Barristera to REVISE THE LISTS OF ELECTORQ, in Parliamentary Elections within the North Wales Circuit, will make a Circuit and hold Courts for Revis- ing the Lists of Parliamentary Electors, County Electors,and Parochial Electors, and also of the Separate List of Persons entitled to be Elected Members of the County Council of the County of Chester, though not entitled to be on the County Electors Roll of the said County, for the KNUTSFORD DIVISION OP THE COUNTY OF CHESTER, at the several times and places following, that is to say— ON TUESDAY, the 10th day of September next, at 11.30 o'clock in the Forenoon, at the National School, Disley, for the several Parishes in the following Polling Districts, viz. : —DISLEY POLLING DISTRICT-131step and Lyme Handley. NEWTOWN POLLING DISTRICT - Newtown, Vi4LALLBY BRIDWI POLLING DlSTRlCT—Kettleahulme. Tazall, and Yeardsley-oum-Whalley. c• ON TUESDAY. tbe 10th day of September next at 2.45 o'clock In the Afternoon, at the News Room, Poynton, for the several Parishes in the following Polling District, viz. —POYNTON-WITII-WOIITH POLLING DISTRICT— Poynton-With-Worth and Woodford.</p>
        <p>ON WEDNIISDAY, the 11th day of September next, at 11.30 o'clock in the Forenoon, at the Sunday School, 801 l log- ton, for the several Parishes in the following Polling Dis- tricts, viz.: BOLLINGTON POLLING DISTItIOT Bollington, formerly the Parishes of Bolllngton and Kerridge, and Pott Shrigley. RAINOW POLLING DISTRICT— Macclesfield Forest and Rainow.</p>
        <p>ON WRDNUSDAY, the 11th day of September next. at 2.15 o'clock in the Afternoon, at the Legh Arms (late Black Boy Inn) Prestbury, for the several Parishes in the following Polling Districts, viz. ADLINGION POLLING DISTRIOI —Adlington and Newton. PtitliThllla POLLING DIE- TRIOT—ButIey, Pallibroome,R3ttram St. Andrew, Prestbnry, , Tytherington and Upton.</p>
        <p>ON THURPDA,Y, the 12th day of September next, at 11 o'clock In the forenoon, at the Drill Hall, Wilmslow, for the several Parishes In the following Polling District, viz. : WILMSLOW POLLING} DISTRICT—BoIIInfee, Stval and Wilmslow.:</p>
        <p>ON FRIDAY. the 13th day of September next, at 11 o'clock in the Forenoon, at the Public Hall, Alrlerlev Bdge, for the several Parishes in the following Foiling District viz. . ALD SRLBY POLLING DISTRICT—ALierIey Edge,Alderley Nether, Alderley Over. Chorley and Warford Great. ON SATURDAY, the 14th day of SeptFrnber neat. at 11.30 o'clock in the Forenoon, at the National School, Siddington, for the several Parishes in the following Polling District,viz. . SIDDINGTON POLLING 018 tßlCT—Capesthorne,Chelford Marton, Siddingtotr, Sneleon, Somerford Booths, With ington Lower and Withington Old.</p>
        <p>ON SATURDAY, the 10th day of September next, at 2.15 o'clock in the Afternoon,at the Club Room of the Bull's Head Hotel. Holmes Chapel, for the se,eral Parishes and parts or Parishes In the following Polling District, viz. : HOtsMRS CHAPHL POLLING DlSTRlOT—Brereton-curn-Stnethwiok, Byley, that part of the Parish formerly known a, Byley-cum- Yatehouse ; Churzh Hulme, Cotton, Cranage, Davenport. Kerminchism, Leere, Somerford. that part of the Parish formerly known as Sornerford-cum-Radnor ; Sproston, that part of the Pa-ish formerly known as Alooresbarrow-cum- Parme ; Sproston, that part of the Parish formerly known as Sproston ; Swettenham and Two:clog.</p>
        <p>ON MONDAY the 16th day of September neat. at 10.15 o'c'ook in the Forenoon at the Sessions House, Knutsford, for the several Parishes In the following Polling Districts, viz : ARTON-BY-BUDWORTH POLLING DI3TRICT— A,ton•by-Bulworth, Crowley and Pick mere. KNUTSFORD POLLING DISTRICT—Heston, Knutsford, Mere. Oilerton. Tabley Inferior. Tabley Superior,Tatton and Toft. MOBFIR It- LIIY POLLING DISTRICT—Martball-cum-Warf9rd and Mobbewley. OFBR PBOVIIR POLLING DISTRICT—BIack - den, Goostrey-cum-Barnshaw, and Peoyer Superior. ON MONDAY, the 16th day of September next, at 2.30 o'clock in the Afternoon, at the Club Room of tire Bl.ck Greyhound Inn, Lostock Grahm, for the several Parishes and part of a Parish in the following Polling Districts, viz : ALLOSTOCK POLLING DIST lOT A llostosit, Peov -r Inferior and Peoyer Nether. LOSTOCK GIRAL AM POLL- ING DISTrIICT—Lach Dennis, Lostock Gralam, Plumbley Radheatb, and Whatcroft, that part of the Parish formerly known as Shiptrook. OR TURSDAY, the 17th day of September neit, at 11.15 o'clock in the Forenoon, at the Large Room, Grappenhall, for the several Parishes in the following Polling Diitrict viz : GR APPIINHA LL POLLING D STRICT —Grappenhall Latchford Without and Warrington, that part within the the Geographical County of Chester.</p>
        <p>ON TUESDAY, the 17th day of September next, at 2.15 o'clock in the Afternoon, at the Hall Cafe, Victoria Square, Stockton Heath, for the sere-al Parishe‘ in the following Polling District', viz: APPLR [ON POLLING DISTRICT —Appleton with Holt and Stratton: STOCKTON 118A.Til POLLING DISTRIC r—Stockton Heath, Walton Inferior and Walton Superior.</p>
        <p>ON WEIDNESDAY. the 18th day of September next at 11.45 o'clock in tne Forenoon, at the Magistratss' Court House, Daresbury, for the several Parishes to the following Polling Districts, viz: DARHSBURY POLLING DISTRICT —Acton Grange, Daresbnry, Hatton, Kekewick, Moore, Newton-by-Daressiury and Preston-o'-th'- WHITLHY POLLING DlSTRlOT—Antrobus. Seven Oaks, Whitley Inferior and Whitley Superior, and for all and every the Parishes, Townships and places Of any) within the said Knutsiord Division of the County of Chester, for whica Courts to revise the Parliamentary Electors' Lists, County Hlectors' Lists, and Parochial Electors' Lists, therein, have not herein before been appointed. At the Courts for such of the above-mentioned Parishes or parts of Parishes as are situate within the Parlianantar Borough of Warrington. the Barrister will, under the stove notice, revise the Ownership Lists only for such Parishes or parts of Parishes. All Overseers and other persons whose attendance may be necessary are hereby required to attend the said Courts at the several times and places aforesaid, at which the Lists of their respe2tive Parishes are hereby appointed to be revised, and all Overseers are required to product in Court the Rate Books of their respective Parishes, ontaining the Poor Hates made and allowed during the period between the sth day of January, 1906, and the 15th day of July, 191.7, and to bring with them copies of their Lists, end all Notices of Claims and Objeetione. and other PapPrs they have received concerning the Registration of Parliamentary Hlectnrs for the Knutsford Division, and County and Parochial Blectors of the said County of Chester,</p>
        <p>REGINALD POTTF, Clerk of the Cheshire County Council. Ckcster, 15th August, 1937.</p>
