        <p>In connection with the Runcorn (F and G) Companies of the 2nd Vol. Battalion Cheshire Regiment, the first annual athletic sports were held on Saturday, on the newly-acquired drill field at the end of Norman-road. The prizes were a very handsome collection, and proved enticing enough to attract sOme 200 entries. There was a fair attendance. The excellent band of the Volunteers who had their silver cup on view, played a capital pro- gramme during the afternoon. Band-Sergeant J. Walker conducted.</p>
